<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Master English vocabulary (SC-3). This is the single source of truth for the app's UI vocabulary and
  the seed for the tokenization convention the exemplar plans (18-05/06/07) and Phase-22 backfill extend.

  ## Key convention
  - Visible labels / titles / body:  <area>_<element>   e.g. printstatus_title, finetune_motion_label
  - contentDescription (a11y) keys:  cd_<thing>          e.g. cd_back  (TalkBack-only, never shown)
  - <area> = the screen/feature owning the string (printstatus, finetune, spool, common, …).

  ## Scope boundary (IN / OUT — see parallel_dinghy/phase-tokenization-staging.md)
  IN  = APP vocabulary authored by us (labels, titles, actions, status words, a11y descriptions).
  OUT = pass-through DATA — filenames, console output, macro params, raw Moonraker fields — those are
        rendered VERBATIM and are NEVER given string keys.

  This file establishes the file + convention + a representative starter set (incl. the required
  format-arg and plurals proofs). Per-screen keys are ADDED by the exemplar plans; the ~240-literal
  backfill is Phase-22 (the detekt baseline from 18-01 tolerates the not-yet-tokenized literals).
-->
